All 8 list operations are implemented and verified:

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `append(list1, list2)` | Adds all items from list2 to the end of list1 |
| `concat(lists)` | Flattens a series of lists into one |
| `filter(function, list)` | Returns items where predicate is True |
| `length(list)` | Counts items without using `len()` |
| `map(function, list)` | Applies function to each item |
| `foldl(function, list, initial)` | Reduces from left to right |
| `foldr(function, list, initial)` | Reduces from right to left |
| `reverse(list)` | Returns items in reversed order |

All implemented without built-in functions (`len()`, `list.extend()`, slicing, etc.) — using only loops and basic `+` for list construction.
